<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linyanti</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Linyanti was the capital of the Kololo kingdom in the mid-19th century, on the Linyanti river in the swamp country of the present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>. The Kololo king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebetwane">Sebetwane</a> ruled from there over the conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a> reached Linyanti in 1851 and 1853, and it was the starting point of his journeys to the Atlantic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> coasts.</p></div>
